Added `--since YYYY-MM-DD` to tools/report.py: since(rows, day) keeps the rows dated on or after the day, and the option goes before or after the path. A day that is not exactly YYYY-MM-DD or not a real date is a usage error: one line naming it on stderr, the usage line, nothing on stdout, exit 64. Tests cover a day inside the data, the day of an order, a day after every order, malformed days and --since with no day. Changed only tools/report.py and tests/test_report.py. python3 -m unittest discover -s tests: 7 tests OK.

Not covered: nothing.
